                    <div class="editarea"><h2>Listing Rules</h2>
<p>NSX Listing Rules are used by NSX listed entities and it is recommended that they are read in conjuction with NSX's Practice Notes.</p>
<div class="f-w-table">
<table>
    <tbody>
        <tr class="sub-header">
            <td align="left">Document</td>
            <td style="text-align: center;">For Issuers</td>
            <td width="65">Type</td>
            <td width="90">Open</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="alt">
            <td align="left">NSX Market Listing Rules - Effective Date 4 July 2018</td>
            <td style="text-align: center;">All</td>
            <td width="65">
            <p class="fa fa-1x fa-color-rust fa-file-pdf">&nbsp;</p>
            </td>
            <td width="90"><a class="btn-blue small" href="/documents/listing_rules/NSX-Listing-Rules.pdf" target="_blank">Open</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="alt">
            <td align="left">Operating Rule Definitions - Effective Date 23 November 2020</td>
            <td style="text-align: center;">All</td>
            <td width="65">
            <p class="fa fa-1x fa-color-rust fa-file-pdf">&nbsp;</p>
            </td>
            <td width="90"><a class="btn-blue small" href="/documents/listing_rules/NSX-Operating-Rules-Definitions.pdf" target="_blank">Open</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td align="left">Sample NSX Compliant Constitution</td>
            <td style="text-align: center;">All</td>
            <td width="65">
            <p class="fa fa-1x fa-color-rust fa-file-word">&nbsp;</p>
            </td>
            <td width="90"><a class="btn-blue small" href="/documents/issuers/NSX%20Standard%20Company%20Constitution.doc" target="_blank">Open</a></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h2>Practice Notes</h2>
<p>NSX issues practice notes to promote commercial certainty, reduce costs to business and assist market participants. As a practice note is only a guide to NSX practice, issuers are advised to contact NSX to discuss their particular circumstances and the application of the listing rules.</p>
<p>NSX may replace practice notes at any time. Issuers should contact NSX to ensure they have the latest version of a practice note.</p>
<p>NSX cannot give legal advice to issuers and recommends that they consider taking advice from a qualified <a href="/listing/nominated-adviser/">Nominated Adviser</a>.</p>
<div class="f-w-table">
<table>
    <tbody>
        <tr class="sub-header">
            <td width="30">Note</td>
            <td align="left">Document</td>
            <td width="65">Type</td>
            <td width="90">Open</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="alt">
            <td width="30">1</td>
            <td align="left">Issuer Fees</td>
            <td width="65"><p class="fa fa-1x fa-color-rust fa-file-pdf">&nbsp;</p></td>
            <td width="90"><a class="btn-blue small" href="/documents/practice_notes/PN01-ListingFees.pdf" target="_blank">Open</a></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td width="30">2</td>
            <td align="left">Trading, Business &amp; Settlement Day Calendar | <a href="/regulation/exchange/trading-hours-and-calendar/">Previous&nbsp;Calendars</a></td>
